# CLAUDE.md — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

How any agent (or human) works in this project. This file is the **map**; the detail lives in
**`.claude/`** (rules, skills, agents, knowledge base, plans). Everything an agent needs is in the repo,
so a new laptop or a lost chat changes nothing. The workflow itself is described in
`.claude/WORKFLOW.md` (copied from the softonoma-orchestrator plugin at onboarding).

## 0. Prime directive — read `.claude/` first
Before non-trivial work, read:
- `.claude/knowledgebase/README.md` → product, business rules, status, and the module docs you'll touch.
- `.claude/knowledgebase/07-change-log.md` → what was done, newest first: **read only its top** (about
  150 lines); older months live in `07-change-log-archive/` and are searched with grep, never read whole.
- `.claude/knowledgebase/research/` → existing research for the module (the grounding for a build).
- `.claude/database/database.md` → the data-model index {{(drop if there is no database)}}.
- `.claude/plans/` → one plan file per ticket (`inprogress/<TICKET>.md`); open follow-ups in `CARRY-OVER.md`.
- `docs/SETUP.md` → what a developer's machine needs (env files and their `.example`, accounts). Add to it
  when you introduce one.
- `.claude/rules/` → security · testing · conventions · git · change-log{{ · design-language (UI) · …}}.
  Rules with `paths:` at the top load only when you touch their files: read one by hand when you PLAN work
  in its area. Each rule line links its story in `.claude/knowledgebase/lessons/`.

Ground every decision in these. If something is missing, decide sensibly and **write it down** (research
doc or KB file) in the same change.

